        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ollama): models advertise tools when /api/show fails",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users discovering local Ollama models would still see tool support advertised when `/api/show` failed (HTTP error or network throw), so a broken or uninspectable model looked tool-capable in catalog/setup paths.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`buildOllamaModelDefinition` treats missing `capabilities` as optimistic `supportsTools: true`. Failed `/api/show` previously returned `{}`, which left capabilities undefined. This change marks failed inspection with `showInspectionFailed`, keeping three states:\n\n1. `capabilities` omitted (uninspected / successful show without field) → optimistic tools + name heuristics\n2. `capabilities: string[]` (including `[]`) → authoritative show result\n3. `showInspectionFailed` → tools conservative, reasoning name heuristics preserved\n\n## User Impact\n\nLocal Ollama models whose `/api/show` fails no longer advertise tools, while reasoning-named models still keep the established name heuristic during transient inspection failures. A successful show that reports an empty capabilities list remains authoritatively non-tool and non-reasoning.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Layer | Proof | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| L1 | three-state unit matrix + HTTP 404/throw paths | pass |\n| L2 | `buildOllamaProvider` enrich → definition on show fail | pass |\n| L3 | Real `127.0.0.1` HTTP (`/api/tags` 200, `/api/show` 500) + undici `fetch` | pass |\n\nScrapable L3 line:\n\n```text\n[ollama show-fail live proof] base=http://127.0.0.1:56531 model=deepseek-r1:14b showHits=1 supportsTools=false reasoning=true\n```\n\nLocal gates on touched files:\n\n```text\npnpm exec oxfmt --check extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.ts extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts\npnpm exec oxlint extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.ts extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts\n→ 25 passed\n```\n\nHead: `b4ee2b824ec5efa8aef56f406bca12504220ab81`",
